1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,400
(Sheldon:)I love the turn-by-turn voice option.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:06,210
Has it really only been 10 miles?

3
00:00:07,143 --> 00:00:09,973
(Leonard:)I'm turning it on, but just to shut you up.

4
00:00:10,747 --> 00:00:16,147
(Sheldon:)Leonard,
bear left and continue on Interstate 210.

5
00:00:18,088 --> 00:00:21,218
(Sheldon:)Ooh, sounds like that fellow
knows what he's talking about.

6
00:00:21,424 --> 00:00:24,224
(Sheldon:)I'd put on my listening ears if I were you.

7
00:00:24,661 --> 00:00:27,721
- What did you do?
- I found a hack online.

8
00:00:27,931 --> 00:00:31,731
(Sheldon:)I was able to upload MP3 recordings
of my voice to your GPS.

9
00:00:31,935 --> 00:00:34,925
- That is so cool.
- Counterpoint, no, it's not.

10
00:00:36,506 --> 00:00:40,736
(GPS:)Continue on Interstate 210 for five miles.

11
00:00:40,944 --> 00:00:43,744
(GPS:)Here's an interesting fact
about Interstates:

12
00:00:45,148 --> 00:00:46,948
- Really?
- Shh!

13
00:00:47,117 --> 00:00:48,277
(Sheldon:)He said it's interesting.

14
00:00:49,386 --> 00:00:52,086
Interstates are numbered as follows:

15
00:00:52,289 --> 00:00:56,019
(GPS:)Even-numbered routes run east and west.

16
00:00:56,559 --> 00:01:00,189
(GPS:)Odd-numbered routes run
north and south.

